@startuml accounts-and-model-proxy-components
!pragma layout smetana
' ^ use PlantUML's built-in layout engine so this component diagram needs NO
'   external Graphviz/dot install (otherwise strict previewers error here).
' ============================================================================
'  M1 — Accounts + Model Proxy : COMPONENT & DATA-FLOW view
'  Two NEW services sit beside the daemon. Both DEFAULT OFF (desktop unchanged).
'  Read this first, then the sequence diagram (2nd @startuml block below).
' ============================================================================
title M1 — Accounts + Model Proxy (what runs where, and why)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

actor "User" as user

rectangle "BROWSER — web client\n----\nHOLDS: session token ONLY (never a model key)\nfiles: lib/auth.ts, components/SignIn.tsx,\n       App.tsx (sign-in gate), lib/platform.ts" as browser

rectangle "agentd DAEMON  :8790\n----\nThe ENGINE. Holds NO provider keys, NO account data.\ngateway.py:  _handle_conn -> _dispatch -> _chat_send -> _run\ninfrastructure/accounts.py:  resolve / check_budget /\n       report_usage  +  current_account / current_usage (contextvars)\ninfrastructure/llm/model_proxy.py:  apply() retargets calls" as daemon

rectangle "ACCOUNTS SERVICE  :4100\n----\nOUR identity + tab ledger (the 'State plane').\nSQLite tables: accounts / sessions / usage\nfile: deploy/accounts/app.py" as accounts

rectangle "MODEL PROXY  :4000  (independent LiteLLM service)\n----\nHOLDS: the REAL provider keys + a master key.\nEvery hosted model call flows through here = metering chokepoint.\nfiles: model_proxy/custom_auth.py, litellm.config.yaml,\n       run-local.py, Dockerfile" as proxy

cloud "PROVIDERS\nGemini / DeepSeek / Anthropic / ..." as prov

user   --> browser
browser --> accounts : (1) POST /login  =>  session token
browser --> daemon   : (2) WS connect  ?token=<session>\n     then chat.send
daemon  --> accounts : (3) GET /resolve  token -> account\n     GET /budget  (pre-check)\n     POST /usage  (report spend)
daemon  --> proxy    : (4) model call\n     model=litellm_proxy/<m>, api_key=master key
proxy   --> prov     : (5) real provider key
prov    --> proxy    : text + token usage
proxy   --> daemon   : answer
daemon  --> browser  : streamed reply

note bottom of proxy
  WHY a proxy: the real keys live in ONE place, never in the
  daemon or the browser. One chokepoint => every call is counted.
  DEFAULT OFF (no AGENTD_MODEL_PROXY_URL) => the daemon calls
  providers DIRECTLY with your .env key, exactly like desktop today.
end note

note bottom of accounts
  WHY a separate service: a FLEET of daemons shares ONE identity +
  tab. The session token is NOT a model key -- if stolen it can only
  spend that one account's budget, never touch a key or another user.
  DEFAULT OFF => no accounts; the single machine token gates instead.
end note
@enduml


@startuml accounts-and-model-proxy-sequence
' ============================================================================
'  M1 — ONE MESSAGE, END TO END : follows both WHO (identity) and MONEY.
'  Each step is tagged with the file/function where it happens.
' ============================================================================
title M1 — one message end-to-end (identity + metering)

skinparam shadowing false
actor User
participant "Browser\nauth.ts / platform.ts" as B
participant "Daemon\ngateway.py" as D
participant "Accounts :4100\napp.py" as A
participant "Model Proxy :4000\nv2/model-proxy" as M
participant "Provider\nGemini/DeepSeek" as P

== sign in (once) ==
User -> B : email + password
B -> A : POST /login
A -> A : verify password, create a sessions row
A --> B : session token  (sess_...)
note over B : stored in localStorage (lib/auth.ts)

== connect (once per browser session) ==
B -> D : WS connect  ?token=sess_...
D -> A : GET /resolve  (Bearer sess_...)      << _handle_conn
A --> D : { account_id, email, budget_usd }
note over D : admitted AS that account.\nbad / missing token => 4401 REFUSED

== each chat turn ==
User -> B : "hello"
B -> D : chat.send
D -> A : GET /budget/<account>                << _chat_send pre-check
A --> D : over ?
alt tab is maxed
  D --> B : refused: "monthly budget reached"
else within budget
  note over D : _run pins account + a fresh empty tab\non contextvars (infrastructure/accounts.py)
  D -> M : model call, api_key = master key     << model_proxy.apply()
  M -> P : real provider key
  P --> M : text + token usage
  M --> D : answer + usage
  note over D : add_usage(): tab += $cost\nread from the contextvar   << litellm.py
  D --> B : streamed reply
  D -> A : POST /usage  (this turn's total)      << _run finally
  A --> D : new month-to-date spend, over = true/false
end
@enduml
